velope":{"contract":"envelope","group":"documents","checked_by":["writer","server","reader"],"says":"How a document travels, as one file the server stores unopened. Per language, the main envelope holds its words, all its pages and its pictures, with references ready, so reading them takes no other request. A second one holds its other files, and exists only when it has any. These fields are the manifest, written in clear, and all the server reads.","enums":{"envelope_kind":["main","files"]},"values":{"layout":["mark","manifest length","manifest","signature length","signature","index","parts"],"mark":"TENV","lengths":"4 bytes, big endian","index":"The SHA-256 of each part as it travels, 32 bytes each, in order.","main_parts":{"first":"The document as JSON, without its body and its pages, so it can be drawn with the first bytes.","rest":"Its body and its pages as JSON, each page with its own HTML. Laid over first, they make the document.","picture":"One for each picture, after those two, in the order its pictures give. Never compressed."},"files_parts":"One file for each of its files, in the order they give. Never compressed.","who_does_what":{"writer":"It compresses and, when private, seals, on the person's machine.","server":"It reads the manifest and the signature, verifies them and stores the file whole. It never compresses or opens anything.","reader":"It opens and inflates, on the reader's machine."},"compression":{"format":"deflate-raw","writer":"On the person's machine, with the strongest deflate it has. Any deflate opens the same, and text saves the most.","reader":"Native DecompressionStream, into a buffer of exactly open_size. A part that gives more or less does not open."},"sealing":{"link_key":"32 random bytes after the # of the link, in base64url. It never reaches the server and never comes from a password.","commitment":"HMAC-SHA-256 of tisty-envelope-commit and the head, with the link key, compared before opening anything.","envelope_key":"HKDF-SHA-256 of the link key, with the head as salt and tisty-envelope-key as info.","parts":"AES-256-GCM. Its nonce is 12 bytes holding the part's number, from 0, big endian. Its additional data is the manifest.","public":"A public envelope is not sealed: no head, no commitment, and its parts travel as they are squeezed."},"signing":{"certificate":"Ed25519 by the root, over tisty-share.certificate.v1, a zero byte, root, machine and since in seconds, 8 bytes, big endian.","signed":"Ed25519 by the machine, over tisty-share.signed.v1, a zero byte, root, machine, the length of envelope in 8 bytes, big endian, envelope, the SHA-256 of the manifest and the index.","files":"The document's files_hash is the SHA-256 of the files envelope's manifest and index, so one signature answers for both."},"versions":"The same major version opens. A higher one is read as newer, and a lower one as damaged.","reading":"The words are drawn first, and the pictures arrive in the same download. A file is asked for the first time it is opened."},"fields":{"contract":{"type":"text","required":true,"at_least":1,"at_most":32,"says":"The version of these contracts it was written under."},"kind":{"type":"envelope_kind","required":true},"id":{"type":"text","required":true,"at_least":1,"at_most":64},"version":{"type":"whole","required":true,"at_least":1},"from":{"type":"whole","says":"The version it starts from."},"sealed":{"type":"bool","required":true,"says":"False only for what is public."},"head":{"type":"hash","required_when":"sealed","says":"32 random bytes."},"commitment":{"type":"hash","required_when":"sealed"},"parts":{"type":"list","of":"envelope_part","required":true,"at_least":1}},"roles":{"writer":{"seal":{"takes":{"document":"document"},"gives":"envelope"}},"reader":{"open":{"takes":{"envelope":"envelope","key":"key"},"gives":"document"}}},"cases":[{"says":"A sealed main envelope.","value":{"contract":"1.0.0","kind":"main","id":"k7Qm2xPa","version":2,"from":1,"sealed":true,"head":"ylsrD8-8Gn6kHk